1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,154
DengueWatch BD is an open source, citizen project.

2
00:00:04,904 --> 00:00:07,538
Citizens send photos of standing water.

3
00:00:08,288 --> 00:00:12,497
Volunteers clean it up… and everyone can see the progress.

4
00:00:13,117 --> 00:00:19,519
Every report has a photo, a GPS location, the container type, and larvae information.

5
00:00:20,069 --> 00:00:24,063
Reports within twenty five meters are joined into one site.

6
00:00:24,683 --> 00:00:30,534
The open map shows reports by ward, environmental risk, and official case numbers.

7
00:00:31,084 --> 00:00:35,234
Satellites cannot see containers. They only show where to look first.

8
00:00:35,850 --> 00:00:37,403
Each ward has a scorecard.

9
00:00:37,953 --> 00:00:41,962
How many places were found, how many were cleaned, and how fast.

10
00:00:42,583 --> 00:00:47,973
If a city corporation wants, it can appoint an admin and inspectors for each ward.

11
00:00:48,423 --> 00:00:52,683
They get their own work list… and close each place with an on-site photo.

12
00:00:53,283 --> 00:00:55,366
Ward admins get a weekly summary.

13
00:00:55,816 --> 00:00:58,938
And all anonymous data can be downloaded, for free.

14
00:00:59,550 --> 00:01:02,010
Today, volunteers are doing this work.

15
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:06,058
If you want to add your ward… please, contact us.

